# Arcane Adaptation naming Saproling (turn 1), Blood Moon (turn 3), then Life and Limb (turn 5), all layer 4 (CR 613.1d).
# Judged on the whole game (CR 613.8a, 613.8c): Arcane Adaptation and Life and Limb depend on each other, Life and Limb also
# depends on Blood Moon, and Blood Moon on nothing. Ready are Adaptation and Blood Moon; Adaptation is the earliest and
# applies first (CR 613.8b; docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-3): Llanowar Elves are a Saproling. Now Life and Limb and Blood
# Moon depend on each other - Life and Limb would make the Elves a land for Blood Moon, and Blood Moon makes Taiga no Forest
# - and the loop goes in timestamp order: Blood Moon, then Life and Limb. Taiga is a plain Mountain, no creature, tapping
# for {R}; the Elves, made a Forest land after Blood Moon applied, are a 1/1 green Creature Land, Elf Druid Saproling
# Forest, tapping for {G}.

